{"id":"decoplex","title":"Decoplex","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Decoplex","rev":240084,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Decoplex"]}," is an aesthetic that was mostly found in movie theaters in the 1990s and early 2000s. It is the third wave of Art Deco motifs after ",{"t":"a","c":["Disco Deco"],"id":"disco-deco"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Deco-Luxe"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Deco-Luxe"},", but is less focused on luxury and more restrained and more inspired by the 1930s-40s golden age of Hollywood, WPA murals, and early air travel."]}],"sections":[{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["The visuals of the aesthetic evokes a playful and cinematic feeling with the use of neon graphic and accent lighting such as intense neon tubing tracking along molding, signs and geometric ceiling trays to emphasize the scale of large commercial spaces."]},{"t":"p","c":["The color palette consists of vibrant neons, rich jewel tones, or contrasting cool or warm tones diffused with chrome and black accents, along with exaggerated geometry, featuring stylized, oversized Art Deco motifs, often focusing on dramatic ziggurats (stepped pyramids) sweeping vertical pylons and giant chevrons."]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Television / Film"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["The Rocketeer (1991)"]},{"c":["The Player (1992)"]},{"c":["Batman: The Animated Series (1992)"]},{"c":["Batman: Mask of the Phantasm (1993)"]},{"c":["Superman: The Animated Series (1996)"]},{"c":["Pleasantville (1998)"]},{"c":["Futurama (1999)"]},{"c":["The Majestic (2001)"]},{"c":["My Life as a Teenage Robot (2003)"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Video Games"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Grim Fandango (1998)"]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/68/Original_4f20967952070e9d6c923df362a085e3.png/revision/latest?cb=20260522041650","w